---
import LegalLayout from "../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "October 11, 2026";
const effectiveDate = "October 11, 2026";

const sections = [
  { id: "summary", title: "1. Summary" },
  { id: "health", title: "2. Health and activity data" },
  { id: "on-device", title: "3. What stays on your devices" },
  { id: "purchases", title: "4. Purchases" },
  { id: "not-collected", title: "5. What we do not collect" },
  { id: "permissions", title: "6. Permissions" },
  { id: "deleting", title: "7. Deleting your data" },
  { id: "children", title: "8. Children" },
  { id: "changes", title: "9. Changes" },
  { id: "contact", title: "10. Contact" },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Wayfoot Privacy Policy"
  description="What the Wayfoot step counter reads, where it keeps it, and what never leaves your devices."
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
  effectiveDate={effectiveDate}
  sections={sections}
>
  <p>
    This policy covers <strong>Wayfoot</strong>, the step counter published by
    NexUtility for iPhone, iPad, Apple Watch, Android and Wear OS. It adds to
    the general <a href="/privacy">NexUtility Privacy Policy</a>. Where the two
    differ, this page applies to Wayfoot.
  </p>

  <p>
    NexUtility is the trading name of <strong>Ahmet Emre Karaca</strong>, an
    individual developer based in İstanbul, Türkiye, who is responsible for Wayfoot and
    for the data described here.
  </p>

  <h2 id="summary">1. Summary</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Wayfoot has no accounts and no NexUtility server. We never receive your steps.</li>
    <li>Your step count and walking distance are read on your device and shown to you there.</li>
    <li>There are no ads, no advertising identifiers and no analytics or tracking tools in the app.</li>
    <li>The only information that leaves your device is what the app stores need to process a subscription.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="health">2. Health and activity data</h2>
  <p>Wayfoot reads two kinds of data, and only reads them. It never writes health data.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Step count</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Walking and running distance</strong></li>
  </ul>
  <p>Where it comes from depends on the device:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>iPhone, iPad and Apple Watch:</strong> Apple Health (HealthKit), after you allow access.</li>
    <li><strong>Android phones:</strong> Health Connect, after you allow access.</li>
    <li><strong>Wear OS watches:</strong> the watch's own step counter, through Android's physical activity permission.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    This data is used for one purpose: to show you your steps, distance and
    progress towards the daily goal you set, in the app, its widgets and its
    watch apps. It is processed on your device. It is not sent to NexUtility
    or to anyone else, not used for advertising or marketing, not sold, and
    not used to build a profile of you.
  </p>
  <p>
    Health data read from Apple Health is not stored in iCloud by Wayfoot.
  </p>
  <p>
    The use of information received from Health Connect will adhere to the
    <a href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/9888170" rel="noopener">Health Connect Permissions policy</a>,
    including the Limited Use requirements.
  </p>

  <h2 id="on-device">3. What stays on your devices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your settings:</strong> the daily goal and whether distance is shown in kilometers or miles.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>The latest count for the widget:</strong> today's step count and
      your goal are kept on the device so the home screen widget, lock screen
      widget and watch tile can show them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your goal on your watch:</strong> if you use the watch app, the
      daily goal (a single number) is passed between your phone and your watch
      using Apple's or Google's own phone-to-watch connection, so both show the
      same goal. Steps are not passed this way.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Exports:</strong> if you export a CSV file, the app creates it on
      your device and hands it to the share sheet. Where it goes after that is
      your choice.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="purchases">4. Purchases</h2>
  <p>
    Wayfoot Pro is an optional subscription. Payment is handled by Apple or
    Google; we never see your card details. To know whether a subscription is
    active, the app uses <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy" rel="noopener">RevenueCat</a>,
    which receives:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>a random identifier created for this installation of the app (not your name, email or an advertising identifier);</li>
    <li>your purchase history for Wayfoot, as reported by the App Store or Google Play;</li>
    <li>basic technical details needed to deliver the service, such as app version, platform, store country and IP address.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>RevenueCat does not receive any health or activity data from Wayfoot.</p>

  <h2 id="not-collected">5. What we do not collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No name, email address, phone number or account.</li>
    <li>No location. Wayfoot does not ask for location access.</li>
    <li>No contacts, photos, microphone or camera.</li>
    <li>No advertising identifier and no tracking across other apps or websites.</li>
    <li>No analytics or crash-reporting service receives data from the app.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If you email us for support, we receive what you write and your email
    address, and use them only to reply.
  </p>

  <h2 id="permissions">6. Permissions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Apple Health / Health Connect (read steps and distance):</strong> to show your activity.</li>
    <li><strong>Health Connect history:</strong> to show days older than the last 30, if you allow it.</li>
    <li><strong>Health Connect background access:</strong> so the home screen widget can stay up to date while the app is closed, if you allow it.</li>
    <li><strong>Physical activity (Wear OS):</strong> to read the watch's step counter.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can withdraw any of these at any time in the Health app, in Health
    Connect or in your device settings. Wayfoot then stops reading that data.
  </p>

  <h2 id="deleting">7. Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>
    Deleting Wayfoot removes everything the app stored on that device. Your
    steps themselves belong to Apple Health or Health Connect and stay there
    under your control. We hold no copy, so there is nothing for us to delete.
    To ask RevenueCat to delete the purchase record tied to your installation,
    write to <a href="mailto:privacy@nexutility.dev">privacy@nexutility.dev</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">8. Children</h2>
  <p>
    Wayfoot is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly
    collect personal information from them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">9. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If Wayfoot starts handling data differently, we will update this page and
    the date at the top before the change reaches you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">10. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy questions: <a href="mailto:privacy@nexutility.dev">privacy@nexutility.dev</a>.
    Anything else: <a href="mailto:hello@nexutility.dev">hello@nexutility.dev</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
